Package: importABCatlas
Title: Release-Aware Import of Allen Brain Cell Atlas Data into R
Version: 0.2.0.9000
Authors@R: person("Maintainer", "To be completed", role = c("aut", "cre"),
    email = "maintainer@example.org")
Description: Resolves Allen Brain Cell Atlas manifest assets, validates metadata
    joins and exact identifiers, reads selected H5AD expression without whole
    matrix densification, and constructs sparse matrices or optional Seurat and
    Bioconductor objects. Uses an explicitly configured external Python process
    and the official Allen data cache. This release candidate requires live atlas
    and R integration validation before a public release.
License: file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.2.0)
Imports: jsonlite, Matrix, methods, stats, utils
Suggests: testthat (>= 3.1.0), roxygen2, SeuratObject (>= 5.0.0),
    SingleCellExperiment, S4Vectors, SpatialExperiment, SummarizedExperiment
SystemRequirements: Python (>= 3.10), numpy, pandas, scipy, h5py,
    abc_atlas_access; Git for explicit upstream SDK installation
Config/testthat/edition: 3
URL: https://github.com/me37uday/importABCatlas
BugReports: https://github.com/me37uday/importABCatlas/issues
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
Config/roxygen2/version: 8.1.1
